# 
\title{L03.4 Setting up a Deep Learning Workspace}
\subtitle{CSci 560: Deep Learning w/ Python (Chollet) Ch. 3.4}
\maketitle

# Setting up a Deep Learning Workspace


- To do deep learning on a GPU, you have three options:
  1. Buy and install a physical NVIDIA GPU on your workstation.
     - [Dettmer The Best GPUs for Deep Learning in 2023](https://timdettmers.com/2023/01/30/which-gpu-for-deep-learning/)
	 - [CUDA GPU Compute Capability](https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-gpus)
  2. Use GPU instances on Google Cloud or AWS EC2.
  3. Use the free GPU runtime from [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/): https://colab.research.google.com/


